# Hybrid Design Engineering & Anti-Slop Directives
# (Emil Kowalski Physics & Motion + Leonxlnx High-End Taste & Output Discipline)

---

## 1. Motion & Physics Engine (Emil Kowalski Framework)

### Easing & Timing Rules
- **Custom Easing Curves:** NEVER use default browser easings (`ease-in`, `ease-out`). Always use custom curves:
  - Strong Ease-Out (Entrances, Dropdowns, Menus): `cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1)`
  - Strong Ease-In-Out (On-screen movement/morphing): `cubic-bezier(0.77, 0, 0.175, 1)`
  - Natural Spring / Drawer Curve: `cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1)`
- **NEVER use `ease-in` for UI entrances:** `ease-in` starts slow and makes the UI feel sluggish. Always start fast with custom `ease-out`.
- **UI Duration Limits:** Keep UI animations under 300ms:
  - Button active / press feedback: `100ms - 160ms`
  - Tooltips & Popovers: `125ms - 200ms`
  - Dropdowns & Cards: `150ms - 220ms`
  - Modals & Drawers: `200ms - 300ms`
- **Keyboard Actions:** NEVER animate keyboard-driven or repeated actions.

### Buttons & Interactive Tactile Feedback
- **Instant Press Feedback:** Every clickable button/card MUST respond on pointer-down with scale reduction:
  ```css
  .btn, .card-button {
    transition: transform 160ms cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1), background-color 160ms ease, box-shadow 160ms cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);
  }
  .btn:active, .card-button:active {
    transform: scale(0.96) !important;
  }
  ```
- **Origin-Aware Scales:** Never scale in from `scale(0)`. Elements must animate from `scale(0.95)` with `opacity: 0`.

---

## 2. High-End Visual Design & Taste (Leonxlnx Framework)

### Anti-Slop Directive
- **Ban Generic Boilerplates:** Never output generic, flat, or template-looking UI. Every layout must look like a $150k+ custom agency engineering build.
- **Serene Whitespace & Breathable Layouts:** Give components generous padding and margins. Avoid tight, crammed cards.
- **Color Contrast & Soft Ambient Glows:** Use calm, high-contrast typography hierarchy paired with soft, highly-diffused ambient glows (`box-shadow: 0 0 24px var(--glow)`).
- **Nested Bezel Architecture (Doppelrand):**
  - **Outer Shell:** Wrapper with subtle background (`rgba(255,255,255,0.03)`), hairline border (`rgba(255,255,255,0.08)`), generous padding, and concentric rounded corners (`rounded-[2rem]`).
  - **Inner Core:** Content enclosure with inner highlight (`box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.12)`).

---

## 3. Full Output Enforcement (Leonxlnx Framework)

- **Zero Truncation / Zero Placeholders:** TREAT EVERY CODE TASK AS PRODUCTION-CRITICAL.
- **Banned Shortcuts:**
  - In code blocks: `// ...`, `// rest of code`, `// implement here`, `// TODO`, `/* ... */`, `// similar to above`, `// add more as needed`
  - In prose: "I'll leave this as an exercise", "the rest follows the same pattern", "for brevity"
- **Requirement:** Deliver 100% complete, unabridged, copy-paste ready production files.

---

## 4. Master Design Reference Table

| Before | After | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `transition: all 300ms` | `transition: transform 160ms cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1)` | Avoid `all`; specify exact property and strong ease-out curve |
| `transform: scale(0)` | `transform: scale(0.95); opacity: 0` | Physical objects don't spawn from nothing |
| Crammed 12px padding | Generous 24px - 32px padding with breathable whitespace | Gives the UI a luxury, unhurried, expensive feel |
| Harsh 1px solid gray border | Semi-transparent hairline shadow `inset 0 1px 0 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.12)` | Subtle glass depth without harsh borders |
| `// ... rest of code` | Full unabridged implementation | Production enforcement; zero incomplete code |
